Patch for Wine's wined3d.dll and d3d11.dll (Wine 11.18) so that Direct3D 11
at feature level 9_x runs SM4 shader code on macOS, on the Vulkan renderer
over MoltenVK or the OpenGL one.

macOS stops at OpenGL 4.1, so wined3d caps every D3D11 device at 9_3, even
for games that ask for 11_x. At 9_x, wined3d ignored the SM4 code and
signatures and only used Aon9 (SM2) code, which Wine's compiler never emits
and whose constants the GL backend never receives from D3D11; games render
black. The SM4 GLSL path also required EXT_shader_integer_mix (GL 4.5), used
only by ftoi/ftou. d3d11 gives a context state the device's own level when
none of the requested levels is available: d2d1 asks for 10_0 only, so
Direct2D games never started.

The launcher picks wined3d's Vulkan renderer on macOS, which MoltenVK runs
on Metal. Metal has no geometry shaders, so that renderer stops at 9_3 too.
On MoltenVK, wined3d leaves out the host-memory handle type Wine adds to
every buffer and image of a 32-bit process, which MoltenVK rejects.

The SM4 and GLSL changes are taken from ctr2-uwp-shim. Built by
scripts/build-wined3d.sh; see docs/building.md.

